	(text "One 5-way port, two kinds of sensor. Analog (a ratiometric 0..3.3 V part): its output goes through 10k/100n (~160 Hz)" (at 780.58 115.57 0)
		(effects (font (size 1.4 1.4)) (justify left bottom))
		(uuid "6806d253-85b4-5047-87ed-2fc039757f86"))
	(text "into AIN1 = P0.03; the 10k also limits what a 5 V sensor plugged in by mistake can push into the pin's clamps. I2C (a" (at 780.58 118.23 0)
		(effects (font (size 1.4 1.4)) (justify left bottom))
		(uuid "cd998304-a124-59b6-9a78-683afa051679"))
	(text "digital barometric or gauge sensor): 4.7k pull-ups on 3V3_SENS, so an unpowered sensor is not back-fed through them." (at 780.58 120.89 0)
		(effects (font (size 1.4 1.4)) (justify left bottom))
		(uuid "63058996-eb5b-5928-ade1-173047990831"))
	(text "The nRF52840 puts TWIM on any pins." (at 780.58 123.55 0)
		(effects (font (size 1.4 1.4)) (justify left bottom))
		(uuid "514c42bb-1459-52b5-855d-6149df952907"))
